{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790346890,"nonce":"jXd53NQlONjUjS29ON/uFbbQTHI=","title":"Match lowering treats pattern kinds it does not implement as always matching","message":"translate_pattern_test (crates/compiler/src/ssa.rs) returns a constant true for every TypedPattern kind without an arm, among them Slice, Guard, Map, View, When, Box and Regex, so an arm using one of them is taken unconditionally. Related gaps in the same code:\n\n- extract_pattern_recursive has no Or arm, so a binding under an Or pattern is never written.\n- The Array test indexes positionally with no length check, so for `[first, .., last]` the last element is tested at index 2.\n\nUnlowered kinds should be refused with a diagnostic until each is implemented. Python's match (e9086df7a988adbd490fd072b65be7ffa70295a5b4aaecc653b39fd078d4ce51) will need Slice, Map and Or bindings.","files":null}]}